2026-04-05 09:13:07.529 | 24908 (24908) | DEBUG    | Model request part: {"tool_name": "open_files", "content": ["Successfully opened memory-bank/performanceOptimizations.md:\n\n````markdown\n   0 # Performance Optimizations - Arkan\n   1 \n   2 *Last Updated: March 2026*\n   3 \n   4 ## React Rendering Optimizations (March 2026)\n   5 \n   6 ### **Atomic State Selectors**\n   7 - **Purpose**: Minimize component re-renders when using Zustand global stores.\n   8 - **Mechanism**: Use narrow, atomic selectors (`useStore(state => state.value)`) instead of monolithic destructuring.\n   9 - **Impact**: Significant reduction in Virtual DOM diffing overhead for logic-heavy pages like the Report Builder.\n  10 \n  11 ### **Component Memoization**\n  12 - **Purpose**: Prevent unnecessary re-renders of complex document previews and forms.\n  13 - **Implementation**: Wrapped `ReportResults`, `TableOfContentForm`, and `ReportSteps` in `React.memo`.\n  14 - **Benefit**: Ensures that document preview only re-renders when the actual content or active panel changes.\n  15 \n  16 ### **DI Resolution Efficiency**\n  17 - **Purpose**: Minimize service resolution overhead in the UI layer.\n  18 - **Implementation**: Created a `useService(token)` hook that utilizes `useMemo` to cache resolved instances from the `tsyringe` container.\n  19 \n  20 ## Agent Lab Performance Enhancements\n  21 \n  22 ### **Caching Strategy Implementation**\n  23 \n  24 #### 1. **Multi-Layer Caching Architecture**\n  25 - **SQLite Database**: Primary data source with optimized queries\n  26 - **API Response Caching**: Browser-level caching with 5-minute expiry\n  27 - **localStorage Cache**: Client-side persistence for offline capability\n  28 - **Search Result Caching**: In-memory caching of search queries for instant responses\n  29 \n  30 #### 2. **Cache Configuration**\n  31 ```typescript\n  32 const CACHE_EXPIRY_MS = 5 * 60 * 1000; // 5 minutes\n  33 const CACHE_KEY = 'arkan_agents_cache';\n  34 const LAST_FETCH_KEY = 'arkan_agents_last_fetch';\n  35 ```\n  36 \n  37 ## RAG System Performance Enhancements\n  38 \n  39 ### **Multi-Layer Caching Architecture**\n  40 \n  41 #### 1. **Embedding Cache**\n  42 - **Purpose**: Avoids re-generating vector embeddings for the same text.\n  43 - **Mechanism**: In-memory LRU (Least Recently Used) cache.\n  44 - **Impact**: Saves ~50-100ms per cached embedding, reduces Ollama API load.\n  45 \n  46 #### 2. **Search Result Cache**\n  47 - **Purpose**: Caches complete search results for identical queries.\n  48 - **Mechanism**: In-memory LRU cache with a 1-hour TTL.\n  49 - **Impact**: Provides instant results (<15ms) for repeated searches, reducing latency by over 90%.\n  50 \n  51 ### **Re-ranking Strategies**\n  52 - **Purpose**: Improves search quality without significant performance cost.\n  53 - **Strategies**:\n  54     - **Hybrid (Default)**: Combines semantic similarity, keyword matching (BM25), and recency for balanced results.\n  55     - **Cross-Encoder**: Most accurate but slower, used for precision-critical tasks.\n  56 - **Impact**: Better result ordering with minimal overhead.\n  57 \n  58 ### **Database Performance (Qdrant)**\n  59 - **Vector Indexing**: Uses HNSW (Hierarchical Navigable Small World) for fast and scalable similarity search.\n  60 - **Payload Indexing**: Indexes on metadata fields (`projectId`, `userId`, `type`) for efficient filtering.\n  61 - **Batch Operations**: Indexing and uploads are batched to maximize throughput.\n  62 - **Impact**: Search latency consistently under 100ms for filtered queries.\n  63 \n  64 ### **API Optimizations**\n  65 - **Streaming Responses**: Used for real-time benchmark results in the admin demo.\n  66 - **Health Checks**: Efficient health check endpoint (`/api/rag/health`) for monitoring without heavy load.\n  67 - **Optimized Payloads**: Minimal data transferred between client and server.\n  68 \n  69 ### **Performance Metrics Achieved**\n  70 \n  71 #### **RAG System**\n  72 - **P50 Search Latency**: < 100ms (uncached), < 20ms (cached)\n  73 - **P95 Search Latency**: < 200ms (uncached)\n  74 - **Indexing Throughput**: ~50-100 chunks/second\n  75 - **Cache Hit Rate**: Target > 70% in production scenarios\n  76 \n  77 #### **Agent Lab**\n  78 - **Initial Load**: < 50ms (from cache)\n  79 - **API Fallback**: < 500ms\n  80 - **Search Speed**: < 10ms (for cached searches)\n  81 \n  82 ## PPTX Export Performance Enhancements\n  83 \n  84 ### **Document Generation Optimization**\n  85 \n  86 #### 1. **Height Calculation Performance**\n  87 - **Smart Caching**: Height calculations cached for repeated elements\n  88 - **Optimized Algorithms**: Improved text measurement with better line counting\n  89 - **Safety Margins**: Prevent recalculation loops with built-in safety buffers\n  90 - **Minimum Heights**: Eliminate zero-height elements that cause layout issues\n  91 \n  92 #### 2. **Text Processing Optimization**\n  93 ```typescript\n  94 // Enhanced text splitting with performance focus\n  95 const splitRunsByHeight = (\n  96   allRuns: PptxGenJS.TextProps[],\n  97   availableHeight: number,\n  98   styles: PptxStyleOptions\n  99 ) => {\n 100   // Sentence-boundary splitting for better performance\n 101   // Word-level fallback only when necessary\n 102   // Cached calculations for repeated patterns\n 103 }\n 104 ```\n 105 \n 106 ### **Export Reliability Improvements**\n 107 - **Error Recovery**: Graceful degradation for failed content (images, tables).\n 108 - **Input Validation**: Early validation of markdown and image URLs.\n 109 - **Content Sanitization**: Clean content processing with error boundaries.\n 110 - **Impact**: 95% reduction in export failures from malformed content.\n 111 \n````", "Successfully opened memory-bank/README.md:\n\n````markdown\n   0 # \ud83e\udde0 Arkan Memory Bank - README\n   1 \n   2 ## Overview\n   3 \n   4 This directory, `memory-bank`, serves as the persistent, long-term memory for the AI development agent working on the **Arkan** project. It contains comprehensive documentation about the project's context, architecture, progress, and technical decisions.\n   5 \n   6 The purpose of this memory bank is to ensure the AI has a deep and accurate understanding of the project, enabling it to make informed decisions, maintain code quality, and follow established patterns consistently.\n   7 \n   8 ---\n   9 \n  10 ## \ud83d\udcda File Index\n  11 \n  12 Below is an index of the files within this directory and their specific purpose.\n  13 \n  14 ### 1. `activeContext.md`\n  15 - **Purpose**: Provides a real-time snapshot of the current development state.\n  16 - **Contains**:\n  17   - Recently completed features.\n  18   - Current development priorities (High, Medium, Low).\n  19   - Active challenges and technical hurdles.\n  20   - Key metrics being tracked.\n  21 \n  22 ### 2. `productContext.md`\n  23 - **Purpose**: Defines the \"what\" and \"why\" of the Arkan project from a business and user perspective.\n  24 - **Contains**:\n  25   - Product vision and mission.\n  26   - Target audience and market.\n  27   - Core product features, including the RAG system.\n  28   - Competitive advantages and unique value propositions.\n  29   - Business model and revenue streams.\n  30 \n  31 ### 3. `techContext.md`\n  32 - **Purpose**: A high-level overview of the technologies and architectural patterns used in the project.\n  33 - **Contains**:\n  34   - Complete technology stack (Frontend, Backend, AI, Database).\n  35   - RAG system architecture overview.\n  36   - State management strategy (Zustand, React Query).\n  37   - Security and performance patterns.\n  38 \n  39 ### 4. `systemPatterns.md`\n  40 - **Purpose**: A deep dive into the specific architectural and design patterns implemented in the codebase.\n  41 - **Contains**:\n  42   - Detailed RAG pipeline explanation (Indexing & Retrieval).\n  43   - State management patterns (Zustand vs. React Query).\n  44   - Error handling and security patterns (API guards, Image Proxy).\n  45 \n  46 ### 5. `progress.md`\n  47 - **Purpose**: Tracks the project's history and completion status over time.\n  48 - **Contains**:\n  49   - Development milestones by phase.\n  50   - Feature completion status across different modules.\n  51   - Key technical achievements and code quality metrics.\n  52 \n  53 ### 6. `recentUpdates.md`\n  54 - **Purpose**: A chronological log of significant recent changes, fixes, and feature implementations.\n  55 - **Contains**:\n  56   - Detailed summaries of major updates (e.g., RAG system implementation, state management overhaul).\n  57   - Links to relevant documentation or code.\n  58 \n  59 ### 7. `performanceOptimizations.md`\n  60 - **Purpose**: Documents specific performance enhancements made to the system.\n  61 - **Contains**:\n  62   - Caching strategies for RAG and Agent Lab.\n  63   - Re-ranking algorithms for search quality.\n  64   - Database performance optimizations.\n  65   - API and document generation (PPTX, DOCX) improvements.\n  66 \n  67 ### 8. `projectbrief.md`\n  68 - **Purpose**: A concise, high-level summary of the entire project.\n  69 - **Contains**:\n  70   - Vision and mission.\n  71   - Primary goals and core features.\n  72   - Target audience and business model.\n  73 \n  74 ---\n  75 \n  76 ## Guidelines for Use\n  77 \n  78 - **Consult Before Acting**: Before implementing new features or making significant changes, the AI should consult these documents to ensure alignment with existing patterns and priorities.\n  79 - **Keep Updated**: After implementing major changes, the AI is responsible for updating the relevant files in this directory to reflect the new state of the project.\n  80 - **Use for Onboarding**: These documents serve as the primary source of truth for understanding the project's history, architecture, and current state.\n  81 \n````"], "tool_call_id": "pyd_ai_5630c839b5574fe1bc92733d2a9ae400", "metadata": null, "timestamp": "2026-04-05T09:13:07.528185+00:00", "part_kind": "tool-return"}
